    "id": "train-4833",
    "question": "John wants to start a zoo.  He has 15 snakes.  He has twice as many monkeys as he does snakes.  He has 5 fewer lions than he does monkeys.   John has 8 more pandas than he does lions.  John has 1/3 as many dogs as he does pandas.  How many total animals does John have?",
    "gold": "114",
    "answer": "John has 15 snakes * 2 = <<15*2=30>>30 monkeys.\nJohn has 30 monkeys - 5 = <<30-5=25>>25 lions.\nJohn has 25 lions + 8 = <<25+8=33>>33 pandas.\nJohn has 33 pandas / 3 = <<33/3=11>>11 dogs.\nJohn has 15+30 + 25 + 33 + 11 = <<15+30+25+33+11=114>>114 animals.\n#### 114"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total number of animals John has, we will calculate the number of each type of animal step by step.\n\n1. **Snakes:**\n   John has 15 snakes.\n\n2. **Monkeys:**\n   John has twice as many monkeys as he does snakes.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of monkeys} = 2 \\times 15 = 30\n   \\]\n\n3. **Lions:**\n   John has 5 fewer lions than he does monkeys.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of lions} = 30 - 5 = 25\n   \\]\n\n4. **Pandas:**\n   John has 8 more pandas than he does lions.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of pandas} = 25 + 8 = 33\n   \\]\n\n5. **Dogs:**\n   John has \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) as many dogs as he does pandas.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of dogs} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 33 = 11\n   \\]\n\n6. **Total number of animals:**\n   To find the total number of animals, we sum the number of each type of animal:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total number of animals} = 15 + 30 + 25 + 33 + 11\n   \\]\n\n   Let's add these step by step:\n   \\[\n   15 + 30 = 45\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   45 + 25 = 70\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   70 + 33 = 103\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   103 + 11 = 114\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of animals John has is \\(\\boxed{114}\\).",
